  "family_notes": {
    "K": "common-law system. Courts enforce the written words closely and follow precedent, so spell out liability caps, termination and governing law.",
    "C": "civil-law system. The civil code fills gaps and courts can cut back unfair terms; penalty and non-compete clauses are often reduced.",
    "M": "mixed legal system. Common-law and civil-law rules can both apply, sometimes by region, so name the governing law and courts explicitly.",
    "I": "Islamic-law principles can apply alongside statute. Interest and some penalty clauses may not be enforceable; fixed fees are safer."
  }
}
